                "reply_count": 0,
                "retweet_count": 68,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "Congress passed a GOP health care bill that will not extend ACA subsidies.\n\nAs a result, 22 million Americans will see their health care premiums skyrocket next year.\n\nThis is only possible because Congress has failed to pass Medicare for All. Through legislation that affirms health care as a human right, we can guarantee that every single person has access to the care that they need.\n\nOur health and well-being cannot continue to be subject to the whims of insurance companies.\n\nPeople in St. Louis already pay too much for their health, vision, and dental insurance as is. Our communities need access to free, universal, and accessible care. This must include abortion, maternity care, and comprehensive care for our seniors, and more.\n\nWhen I\u2019m back in Congress, we\u2019ll fight for a health care system that puts people over profit, as we build an economy that works for all of us, where everyday people can afford to not only survive, but thrive.",
